    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d503">

                <pb facs="0622" n="542" xml:id="pg542"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr.
                            Loomis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-02-14"><hi rendition="#italic">February 14,
                        1901</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 394.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I confirm your telegram of the 12th instant
                    reporting the Venezuelan Government’s protest against the presence of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Scorpion</hi> in the Orinoco River, and the Department’s
                    telegraphic reply of the 13th instant.</p>
                <p>I inclose for your information copy of the Navy Department’s memorandum of the
                    13th instant relative to the precedents for the visits of United States war
                    vessels to the Orinoco River.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d503-a1.xml" xpointer="d503-a1"/>
